//! Structured concurrency support types.
//!
//! A plain call waits for its result. `fork expression` creates a `Task<T>`;
//! `await task` returns `T`, and awaiting `Vec<Task<T>>` returns `Vec<T>`.
//! Await preserves application values, including `Result` values.
//!
//! `scope { ... }` yields its body's value after waiting for child tasks and
//! cleanup. `scope within duration { ... } handle failure { ... }` adds a
//! deadline and recovery after cleanup. Ordinary `Err` values remain values;
//! structured faults and cancellation determine scope failure and sibling
//! cancellation. Parent cancellation propagates to the enclosing scope.
//!
//! `ScopeError<E>` below is a legacy aggregation record. Current scope recovery
//! uses the built-in `ScopeFailure`; it does not automatically aggregate every
//! application's `Err` into this record.

/// Legacy aggregation record; current scope recovery uses `ScopeFailure`.
pub type ScopeError<E> {
    primary: E,
    also_failed: Vec<E>,
    cancelled_count: i64,
}
